<title>UK: Easier sterling sends UK wheat futures up.</title>
<headline>Easier sterling sends UK wheat futures up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A weaker pound sterling before and after an announcement of a UK general election on May 1 sent UK LIFFE wheat futures higher.</p>
<p>By the close, May wheat, which dominated activity, was 1.50 stg up at 101.10 stg. May volume was 423 of a total 669 lots of wheat.</p>
<p>The rise was due to currency &quot;and a bit of carry-over bullish sentiment from last week,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Barley also rose, with November, the most active contract, up 0.25 stg at 93.75. November volume was 25 lots of a total 44 on barley.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
